title: A Joint List?
subtitle: The lists for the Sejm election are open: a joint list, or our own.
new-page: true
tags: pl_event
face-image: img/polish/polish_list_agreement.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && PolishGovernment.listEventDue(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Event parliament.list_agreement (Z — 0.57, items 7 and 8 of the play notes of 5 X 2026). It replaces card 7.7 of the
// card catalogue and keeps its scene ID: two months before the vote PPS proposes one joint list or goes alone; the
// partners answer once by the evaluation of a cabinet offer (technical reference 6.2, 6.5). A proposal costs no action.
// After a refusal the question returns once in the last month of the window, if a list is still possible. The peasant
// bloc without PPS is no longer a decision of PPS.
PolishGovernment.listEventView(Q);
!}

= A joint list?

The Sejm election is held on [+ pl_list_vote +], and the lists close at the end of the month before the vote. Without an agreement PPS stands alone with its full programme and all its own candidates; refusing an alliance brings no bonus.

A joint list counts the votes of its parties together in the seat method, and shares its seats in proportion to their votes. Each party keeps its own club after the election and may vote differently; a list gives no ministry and binds nobody to a later cabinet. Each partner answers once, by the same evaluation as a cabinet offer. A proposal costs no action this month.

- @left_peasant
- @labour
- @centrolew_early
- @alone

@left_peasant
title: A joint list of PPS and PSL Wyzwolenie
subtitle: Land reform with equal access and protection of labour; seats shared in proportion to votes.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.listStatus(Q, 'left_peasant').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_list_left_peasant_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
var record = PolishGovernment.proposeList(Q, 'left_peasant');
Q.pl_list_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_list_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
Q.pl_list_name = PolishGovernment.LIST_OPTIONS.left_peasant.name;
Q.pl_list_retry = !record.accepted && PolishGovernment.listRetryPossible(Q) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: result

@labour
title: A joint list of PPS and NPR
subtitle: The eight-hour day, protection of the unemployed and religious freedom.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.listStatus(Q, 'labour').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_list_labour_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
var record = PolishGovernment.proposeList(Q, 'labour');
Q.pl_list_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_list_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
Q.pl_list_name = PolishGovernment.LIST_OPTIONS.labour.name;
Q.pl_list_retry = !record.accepted && PolishGovernment.listRetryPossible(Q) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: result

@centrolew_early
title: An early Centre-Left of PPS, both peasant parties and NPR
subtitle: A lawful change of government, a social minimum and a land and religious compromise. The Lewica opposes giving up points of the workers' programme.
choose-if: {! return PolishGovernment.listStatus(Q, 'centrolew_early').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_list_centrolew_early_reason +]
on-arrival: {!
var record = PolishGovernment.proposeList(Q, 'centrolew_early');
Q.pl_list_accepted = record.accepted ? 1 : 0;
Q.pl_list_answers = PolishGovernment.describeAnswers(record);
Q.pl_list_name = PolishGovernment.LIST_OPTIONS.centrolew_early.name;
Q.pl_list_retry = !record.accepted && PolishGovernment.listRetryPossible(Q) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: result

@alone
title: We go to the election alone
subtitle: PPS stands with its full programme and all its own candidates; no joint list at this election.
on-arrival: {!
PolishGovernment.listGoAlone(Q);
!}
go-to: alone_result

@result
new-page: true

= The answer

[+ pl_list_answers +]

[? if pl_list_accepted : **[+ pl_list_name +] will stand as one list** at the coming election. ?]

[? if not pl_list_accepted : **No joint list.** PPS keeps its own list. ?]

[? if pl_list_retry : Before the lists close next month, PPS can propose another joint list. ?]

- @root: Continue.

@alone_result
new-page: true

= Our own list

PPS goes to the election alone, with its full programme and all its own candidates.

- @root: Continue.
